Adapted from vLLM
-----------------

peer/peer_moe.py: experts_fp8 is adapted from vLLM's fused_experts_impl
(vllm/model_executor/layers/fused_moe/fused_moe.py at commit a2bcb5657a881a002e79d0adab3c6b5e39436121,
https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm). Copyright contributors to the vLLM project, Apache License 2.0
(peer/LICENSE.vllm). Changes: the activation is GLM's clamped SwiGLU, an expert map restricts the computation to one
GPU's experts, and the Triton tile can be passed in. The rest of peer/ calls vLLM's and FlashInfer's public and
internal functions from the pinned image without copying them.

Used, not included
------------------

routing/build_mix.py fetches prompts to drive the server while expert routes are counted; none of the prompt text
is stored in this repository. The rowmap records only per-expert counts. Sources, with their revisions recorded in
the first line of the generated mix (mix-v1, sha256 9d436e78…): HuggingFaceH4/ultrachat_200k (MIT), CohereLabs/aya_dataset (Apache-2.0), HuggingFaceH4/MATH-500,
openai/openai_humaneval (MIT), google-research-datasets/mbpp (CC-BY-4.0), princeton-nlp/SWE-bench_Lite,
gorilla-llm/Berkeley-Function-Calling-Leaderboard (Apache-2.0), vLLM sources (Apache-2.0) and CPython sources (PSF).
